439	<body>
440		<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
441		<header id="top">
442			<h1>Welcome</h1>
443			<nav aria-label="Page sections">
444				<ul>
445					<li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
446					<li><a href="#examples">Examples</a></li>
447					<li><a href="#resources">Resources</a></li>
448				</ul>
449			</nav>
450		</header>
451		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
452			<section aria-label="Introduction">
453				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
454				<p>
455					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
456					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
457				</p>
458				<p>
459					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
460					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
461				</p>
462			</section>
463	
464			<section aria-labelledby="features">
465				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
466				<ul>
467					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
468					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
469					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
470					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
471					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
472					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
473				</ul>
474			</section>
475	
476			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
477				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
478				<article class="card">
479					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
480					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
481					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
482				</article>
483	
484				<article class="card">
485					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
486					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
487					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> to activate.</p>
488				</article>
489	
490				<article class="card">
491					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
492					<form id="contact-form" novalidate>
493						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked * are required.</p>
494						<div class="field">
495							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
496							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" required aria-describedby="email-help">
497							<span id="email-error" class="error-message"></span>
498							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">For example, name@example.com</small>
499						</div>
500						<div class="field">
501							<label for="message">Message</label>
502							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="message-help"></textarea>
503							<small id="message-help" class="form-hint">Up to 2,000 characters. <span id="message-count">2,000</span> remaining.</small>
504						</div>
505						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
506						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
507					</form>
508				</article>
509	
510				<article class="card">
511					<h3>Live Region Example</h3>
512					<p>Click the button to announce a message using a live region. This demonstrates how screen readers are notified of dynamic updates.</p>
513					<button id="announce" type="button">Announce message</button>
514					<div class="live-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
515						<span id="live-message"></span>
516					</div>
517				</article>
518	
519				<article class="card">
520					<h3>Interactive Counter</h3>
521					<p>This counter demonstrates state management and ARIA live regions for accessible dynamic content.</p>
522					<div class="counter">
523						<button id="decrease" type="button" aria-label="Decrease count by 1">−</button>
524						<output id="count" aria-live="off">0</output>
525						<button id="increase" type="button" aria-label="Increase count by 1">+</button>
526						<button id="reset" type="button" aria-label="Reset count to zero">Reset</button>
527					</div>
528					<div class="live-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
529						<span id="count-message"></span>
530					</div>
531				</article>
532			</section>
533	
534			<section aria-labelledby="resources">
535				<h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
536				<p>Want to learn more about web accessibility and semantic HTML? Check out these resources:</p>
537				<ul>
538					<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WCAG 2.2 Quick Reference<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
539					<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HTML Living Standard<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
540					<li><a href="https://www.a11y-101.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A11y 101<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
541				</ul>
542			</section>
543		</main>
